      "writtenOn": "2017-06-21T00:13:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh hmmm part of the reason I liked \"zipEntry\" was because it matched the name of the class in Python and in Java that refers to a file with a certain location within a zip.\n\nIt seems to me that it\u0027s more informative to tell the reader that the fileMatch/matchEntry/zipEntry type is used for building part of the output zip - it says \"put this content at this file path\" - than the fact that it was generated by doing a text match against the previous zip (and actually the value of fileMatch.name is the newFileName rather than the old fileName anyway)\n\n\nAlternatively I could see \"fileMapping\" being another name for it.",
      "parentUuid": "c3de0ce7_9bc21466",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 14
